      ],
      "source": "https://www.pinetopcc.com/life-at-pinetop/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The club purchased 496 acres, then sold residential lots to fund the golf course and other amenities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pinetopcc.com/life-at-pinetop/history",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Remnants of an early 1900s logging railroad bed can still be seen throughout the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pinetopcc.com/life-at-pinetop/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A former cattle stock‑watering tank behind the fifth green now supplies water for the golf course.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pinetopcc.com/life-at-pinetop/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Developers discovered one of the White Mountains’ best‑producing wells near the twelfth tee, still visible today.",
